{"kind":"assert","text":"gs CLI novice-usability review findings, 2026-08-28 (hugh-requested). Evidence-based review of the `gs` command line for a NOVICE actor with NO MCP access — only ./bin/gs + git. Reviewed cmd/gs, docs/reference/gs, docs/how-to/end-to-end.md, SKILL.md, and exercised the full work loop in a throwaway repo (real durable log untouched). Verdict: the fold's field-level errors are mostly good and read-orientation against the advertised resident is fast, but the CLI is undocumented at point of use and the event-ID ergonomics are a trap.\n\nPRIORITIZED FINDINGS (each backed by a run or file:line):\n1. NO HELP TEXT ANYWHERE (biggest blocker, cheap fix). `gs \u003canything\u003e --help` prints only \"gs: flag: help requested\" and exits 1, because flags() at cmd/gs/main.go:143-147 builds every FlagSet with flag.ContinueOnError AND set.SetOutput(io.Discard) and never sets flag.Usage. An unknown flag prints \"flag provided but not defined: -foo\" with no list of valid flags. No `gs help`, no `gs guide`, no per-command usage. Fix: set.SetOutput(os.Stderr) + real Usage/PrintDefaults per subcommand; -h/--help exits 0 after printing; add `gs help [subcommand]`; usage() footer pointing to docs/how-to/end-to-end.md.\n2. EVENT-ID FORMS SHOWN != FORMS ACCEPTED, and misses are silent or slow. Only the full 89-char git:sha1:\u003cgenesis\u003e#git:sha1:\u003cevent\u003e resolves. gs work prints ellipsis-truncated ids (git:sha1…\u003csuffix\u003e, uncopyable); gs status prints #N. Both are rejected by action commands, and every miss first runs a slow local fold (\"verifying the durable log; this may take a while\") before failing \"event is not in the durable projection\". No prefix resolution, no #N acceptance, no shell completion. Fix (cheap): human work/status/inspect output carries the full canonical ID; not-found error explains the canonical form and that #N is display-only, get the full id from gs work --json. Fix (deeper, design-gated): accept #N and unambiguous hex prefixes/suffixes resolved against the projection BEFORE the slow local fold.\n3. state ACCEPTS GARBAGE BASES SILENTLY AND REPORTS SUCCESS. `gs state --kind request` with no --rests-on, or --rests-on '#1', prints an event id and exits 0; inspect shows the fold ruled it effective with the literal '#1' stored as a basis, or 0 bases. A novice pasting the #N they saw creates a live request stale-from-birth with no warning. Fix (design-gated): validate --rests-on values are well-formed canonical ids resolving in the projection before submit; extend the existing noteDeadRestsOn (main.go:357-358) to unknown bases. NOTE: this overlaps in-flight admission work (claude staleness-policy 769006ed, codex completion-reliability ratify-preflight 4f3310a8) and must coordinate to avoid duplication.\n4. NO gs whoami; work needs an actor but status does not. gs work refuses without --as/GITSEQ_ACTOR (\"no actor identity: pass --as...\"); status runs without one. Identity you can sign as is only inferable from gs actors JSON (\"custody\": true). Fix (cheap): add gs whoami printing resolved actor + local custody identities; work's identity refusal names the custody actors found.\n5. artifact commit not validated until merge. gs state --kind artifact --body commit=\u003cshort sha\u003e succeeds; the full-object-id requirement fires only at merge (main.go:892). Fix (cheap): validate body.commit resolves to a full object id at artifact-filing with the merge path's message.\n6. Some refusals assume deep model knowledge. Field errors are good (mistyped --kind lists valid kinds; request state requires body.conditions; body.to addresses no known actor). But merge/supersede refusals presume the causal model: succession.go:491 \"merge would retire %s at %q, which belongs to another actor and lies outside the reviewed paths\"; fold.go:874 dangling promise has no request; fold.go:804 report cites a request other than the one its promise answers; fold.go:1087 actor may not supersede target. Fix (cheap): append a one-line \"what to do\" + docs pointer to the highest-traffic refusals (merge preflight, report/promise mismatch).\n7. Getting-started is MCP-only; the CLI tutorial is unlinked. docs/getting-started.md assumes MCP tools; the fitting resource docs/how-to/end-to-end.md (empty dir to audited record, 20 gs commands) is excellent but the CLI never points to it. Fix (cheap): gs guide / usage footer linking it.\n\nCHEAP vs DEEP: cheap CLI/help/error changes = #1, #2a, #4, #5, #6, #7 (high value, no design). Deeper/design-gated = #2b id resolution, #3 submit-time basis validation (both interact with the fold's \"a citation resolving to nothing is admitted in silence\" contract). Improvement request rests on this assert."}